# iBasso DC03 Pro — hidraw control endpoint
#
# Grants the active-seat user direct access to the device's HID node, and
# fires the user-level dc03-restore service on attach so dc03 can persist
# the device path and replay stored settings. See docs/design.md.
#
# There is intentionally no detach rule: systemd's SYSTEMD_USER_WANTS
# mechanism only fires user units on `add` events, not on `remove`.
# Empirically: the env var is preserved into the remove event, but
# systemd-udev never instantiates a user unit from it. Stale device.toml
# entries are handled by validate-on-read inside the CLI itself
# (resolve_device_path).

ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="262a", ATTRS{idProduct}=="187e", \
    TAG+="uaccess", TAG+="systemd", \
    ENV{SYSTEMD_USER_WANTS}+="dc03-restore@%k.service dc03-watch@%k.service"
